<section class="section ">
  <div >
    <div class="section__color-wrapper ">
      <div class="container "><div class="content-box content-box--large content-box--text-left content-box--left text-container"><h3 class="heading h2">How it crept up on me</h3><p>It didn't arrive all at once. That's the sneaky part.</p><p>First it was just spring. Then it was spring <em>and</em> fall. Then it was the dry winter air, then the change of seasons, then — somewhere in there — it stopped really having a season at all. The congestion, the pressure headaches "every couple of days," the heavy drip at the back of my throat, the feeling of being slightly underwater all the time.</p><p>It took the small things first. Tasting my coffee. Sleeping through the night. Sitting through a movie without that maddening urge to sniff. And then it took the bigger ones: my patience, my energy, the version of me that used to say yes to things without first running a silent calculation of how stuffed up I'd be.</p><p>I kept telling myself it wasn't a big deal. But living with it <em>every single day</em> — that's a big deal.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</div><div id="shopify-section-template--27702861398296__rich_text_76YNqa" class="shopify-section shopify-section--rich-text"><style>
