  }
</style>

<section class="section ">
  <div >
    <div class="section__color-wrapper ">
      <div class="container "><div class="content-box content-box--large content-box--text-left content-box--left text-container"><h3 class="heading h2">Day 1, Day 2, Day 3</h3><p>I'll be honest — the first time felt strange. New sensation, a little intimidating. (Almost everyone says this. More on that in a second.)</p><p>But then it was over, and I did the thing everyone does: I looked. And I <em>saw</em> what came out. After years of feeling that stuff sitting in my nose, watching it actually leave was — I'm not exaggerating — a little emotional.</p><p><strong>Day 1:</strong> I could breathe through both nostrils for the first time in longer than I could remember.</p><p><strong>Day 2:</strong> I slept. All the way through. No 2 a.m. coughing fit. I woke up and just lay there for a second, almost suspicious of how clear my head felt.</p><p><strong>Day 3:</strong> I caught myself taking a deep breath through my nose without thinking about it. Such a small thing. I nearly cried over it.</p><p>After all those years of feeling resigned to it, even those small wins felt enormous.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</div><div id="shopify-section-template--27702861398296__rich_text_Dp9XaG" class="shopify-section shopify-section--rich-text"><style>
  #shopify-section-template--27702861398296__rich_text_Dp9XaG {--heading-color: 7, 65, 116;
    --text-color: 7, 65, 116;
    --primary-button-background: 151, 168, 227;
    --primary-button-text-color: 7, 65, 116;

    --section-background: 245, 245, 247;
  }
</style>

<section class="section ">
  <div >
    <div class="section__color-wrapper ">
      <div class="container "><div class="content-box content-box--large content-box--text-left content-box--left text-container"><h3 class="heading h2">What I got back</h3><p>It's been a while now, and here's the honest truth: I don't organize my life around my nose anymore.</p><p>I sleep through. I taste my coffee. I sit through a whole dinner without my little purse arsenal. The foggy, underwater, slightly-ashamed version of me from that 2 a.m. night feels like a different person.</p><p>I'm not telling you it's magic, and I'm not telling you to throw out everything your doctor said. I'm telling you that for the first time, I have something that lets me get <em>cleaned out</em> — on my own, at my sink, in under a minute, without reaching for another pill. And that has given me back something I'd quietly grieved: the simple, daily, taken-for-granted feeling of <em>breathing.</em></p><p>If you'd told me on that 2 a.m. night that I'd feel this way, I wouldn't have believed you. That's exactly why I'm telling you now.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</div><div id="shopify-section-template--27702861398296__design_pack_banner_image_simple_4bh4Fw" class="shopify-section DP__banner-image-simple">

